    "q-181624": {
      "dom_id": "step-q181624",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$$\nX={a,b,2,4},\\,Y={n\\in N∣\\,1\\le n<5}\n$$\n\nConsider the sets $X$ and $Y$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $|X|=4$\n- $|Y|=5$\n- $|X|=|Y|$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that finite sets have the same cardinality if and only if they have the same number of elements.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $X$ is a finite set and $|X|=4.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that $Y={1,2,3,4}$ is a finite set and $|Y|=4.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, $X$ and $Y$ are finite sets and  $|X|=|Y|=4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
