    "q-182647": {
      "dom_id": "step-q182647",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$$\nU={5n-4∣\\,n\\in Z},\\,V={4,8,…,40}\n$$\n\nComplete the following reasoning about the sets $W$ and $V$ above:\n\nSince $U$ is {{field-1}} and $V$ is {{field-2}}, we have that {{field-3}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The cardinalities of two sets cannot be equal if one set is finite and the other is infinite.\n\nWith that in mind, notice that \n\n- $U={…,-14,-9,-4,1,6,…}$ is infinite, while\n\n- $V$ is finite where $|V|=10.$\n\nTherefore, $|U|\\ne |V|.$",
